From: aiden build <build@aiden.local>
Subject: [PATCH] diagnose_usb: skip glibc group_member() path on uClibc

diagnose_usb.cpp guards a plugdev-group check with
'#if defined(__GLIBC__) && !defined(__BIONIC__)' and calls the GNU
extension group_member(3) inside it. uClibc-ng defines __GLIBC__ for
source compatibility but does NOT provide group_member(), so the build
fails:

  diagnose_usb.cpp:50:9: error: 'group_member' was not declared in this scope

Exclude uClibc from that branch by adding '&& !defined(__UCLIBC__)'. On
uClibc the function then returns an empty string (the "can't determine
the problem" fallback), which is the correct degraded behaviour.

Aiden-local patch (not from upstream nmeum/android-tools).
---
--- a/vendor/core/diagnose_usb/diagnose_usb.cpp
+++ b/vendor/core/diagnose_usb/diagnose_usb.cpp
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
 // Returns a message describing any potential problems we find with udev, or an empty string if we
 // can't find plugdev information (i.e. udev is not installed).
 static std::string GetUdevProblem() {
-#if defined(__GLIBC__) && !defined(__BIONIC__)
+#if defined(__GLIBC__) && !defined(__BIONIC__) && !defined(__UCLIBC__)
     errno = 0;
     group* plugdev_group = getgrnam("plugdev");
 
